#
# chrony drop-in for the robot AGX — installed at /etc/chrony/conf.d/camera-agx.conf
# deploy time. The same deploy installs camera-time-sync.service so camera-argus-sender
# starts only after this source has disciplined the clock (see both unit files).
#
# The AGX has no internet; its only time source is the host PC over the robot
# LAN, which is internet-disciplined and re-serves. Software timestamping over the
# sub-ms link is ~10-50 us — far below the 33 ms (30fps) / 16 ms (60fps) frame
# budget. iburst = fast lock; short poll = tight tracking on the quiet link.
server @HOST_LAN_IP@ iburst minpoll 2 maxpoll 4

# Step (not slew) a large initial offset, but only in the first few updates after
# chronyd starts. Do the first big correction in a coordinated no-recording window.
makestep 1.0 3
